## A `! str` function with a result: a branch with no value mid-body reports expr.if.4, and the `str`
## tail `if` is no no-result body, so no err.str.4 and no `! Fail` fix.
fn pick(k int) ! str
    x := if k > 0
        print("a")
    else
        1
    if k > 1
        "x"
    else
        "y"

fn main()
    print(pick(2) else "z")
